<title>HUNGARY: IEB Jan-Sept pre-tax profit up at 1.55 bln.</title>
<headline>IEB Jan-Sept pre-tax profit up at 1.55 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ending on Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					  96 Jan-Sept    95 Jan-Sept</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   1,881.7   vs    1,319.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     1,551.1   vs    1,356.9</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total	     81,304.3   vs   57,930.4</p>
<p>    Net interest revenue	     3,092.6   vs    2,493.1</p>
<p>     Interest received		 8,513.8   vs    7,675.1</p>
<p>     Interest paid		     5,421.2   vs    5,182.0</p>
<p>Other revenues from</p>
<p>     banking activity		  4,113.1   vs    1,345.6</p>
<p>Other expenditures</p>
<p>     of banking activity	     3,506.2   vs	523.2</p>
<p>    Other revenue			   19.4   vs	155.4</p>
<p>    Other expenditure		    266.3   vs	934.3</p>
<p>    Costs of banking activity	1,590.7   vs    1,231.1</p>
<p>    Dividend received		     19.8   vs	 14.1</p>
<p>    Result of banking activity     1,881.7   vs    1,319.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Inter-Europa Bank Rt is member of Italy's San Paolo di Bancario group.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
